    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Post-traumatic osteoarthritis of the right hand (M19.141)</content>. Controlled: pain 2 of 10 with daily writing and FIHOA 4 of 30. [S]<list><item>Continue the home program and the gel as needed.</item><item>Hand review at the yearly visit or sooner if pain rises.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Personal history of psychological trauma (Z91.49)</content>. PCL-5 16, down from 24 at intake, and PHQ-9 2 with item 9 scored 0. Watchfulness on the road is proportionate to real past threats and does not limit his work. [S]<list><item>PCL-5 and PHQ-9 at the yearly chronic-care review.</item><item>Return to Dr. Morrison at any time, and trauma-focused psychotherapy if symptoms rise to the probable-PTSD range or he wants it.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Insufficient sleep (Z72.820)</content>. Goal met: about seven hours on most nights. [S]<list><item>Keep the routine.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Consent before each question, examination, and test; chaperone offered</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>He agreed to the questionnaires and the hand examination</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Hand joint examination (range of motion, swelling, alignment, grip)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No tenderness; flexion slightly limited; grip 85 percent of the left</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Hand pain, 0 to 10 numeric rating</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>2 of 10 with daily writing</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Hand function with a validated instrument (FIHOA)</td><td>Each clinical encounter</td><td>Completed today</td><td>FIHOA 4 of 30, recorded in this note</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Hand exercise and joint-protection program</td><td>Ongoing; six hand-therapy sessions over eight weeks, then a home program</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Home program most days</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Topical NSAID tolerance (skin irritation)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No skin irritation; gel once a day or less</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>CBC, creatinine, and blood pressure for chronic oral NSAID use; ALT for chronic acetaminophen</td><td>Every 6 to 12 months, only with chronic oral NSAID or acetaminophen use</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Topical diclofenac only</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>PCL-5 (trauma-related symptom severity)</td><td>At intake and at each chronic-care visit (measurement-based care)</td><td>Completed today</td><td>16, down from 24 at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>PHQ-9 (depression, with item 9)</td><td>At intake and at each chronic-care visit; also the CMID mental-health and coping screen for osteoarthritis</td><td>Completed today</td><td>2, item 9 scored 0</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Sleep hours, sleep diary, and nightmare frequency</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>About seven hours on five or six nights a week; one nightmare in the past month</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Clinical psychology evaluation (structured interview, CAPS-5)</td><td>Once at the start; again if symptoms rise or he wants treatment</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Below the threshold and improving; the door stays open</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Strengths and supports he names</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Working and traveling as he wishes, with travel planned around his safety</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Write for an hour with right-hand pain no higher than 2 of 10. Outcome by 1852-05-19: Met at ten weeks: pain 2 of 10 after an hour of writing [S]</item><item>Sleep at least seven hours on five nights a week. Outcome by 1852-08-18: Met at five months: about seven hours on five or six nights a week; nightmares about once a month [S]</item><item>Track trauma-related symptoms with the PCL-5 and return to psychology if the score reaches the probable-PTSD range or he wants treatment. Outcome by 1852-08-18: PCL-5 24, 19, and 16; no return needed so far [S]</item><item>Every examination, test, and question about his history happens only with his agreement. Outcome by 1852-08-18: Consent recorded at every visit; he declined a back examination at intake, and the offer stays open [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Management of Posttraumatic Stress Disorder and Acute Stress Disorder (2023); Trauma-Informed Care in Behavioral Health Services (Treatment Improvement Protocol 57) (2014); 2019 American College of Rheumatology/Arthritis Foundation Guideline for the Management of Osteoarthritis of the Hand, Hip, and Knee (2019); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, rheumatoid arthritis and osteoarthritis monograph (2026); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Management of Chronic Insomnia Disorder and Obstructive Sleep Apnea (2025); Depression and Suicide Risk in Adults: Screening (2023)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Adult preventive visit in the autumn. Yearly chronic-care review with the PCL-5, PHQ-9, FIHOA, and pain score; sooner for any concern. Next scheduled visit 1852-10-06: adult preventive visit. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
